decision_conditions:
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cycle Store&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted
details of relocation of cycle parking store to the rear garden shall be
submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The cycle
storage shall be made available prior to occupation and shall be retained
thereafter.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Planting&lt;/u&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;All planting, seeding or turfing included in the approved details of
landscaping shall be carried out in the first planting season and first seeding
season following the occupation of the building. Any trees or plants which
within a period of 5 years from the occupation of the building die, are removed
or become seriously damaged or diseased shall be replaced in the next planting
season with others of similar size and species.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Refuse Storage&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;The refuse and waste bins shall be stored at all times, other than on
collection days, within the designated refuse storage areas as shown on the
approved details set out in Condition 2 of this permission.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Restriction of Permitted Development Rights 1&lt;/u&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:32.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General
Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (or any order revoking and
re-enacting that order with or without modification), no development which
would otherwise fall within Classes A, B, D, E and F in Part 1 of Schedule 2
shall take place without the prior permission of the local planning authority.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Precautionary Working Method Statement&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;No development shall take place (including vegetation/site clearance)
until a Precautionary Working Method Statement (PWMS) for protected species has
been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The
PWMS should include, but may not be limited to;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;i&quot;&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;A toolbox
     talk covering the ecology of and legislation which protects species which
     may be present on site, to be delivered to construction personnel by the
     Ecological Clerk of Works (ECoW);&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;A plan
     showing areas of sensitivity and exclusion zones;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Details of
     where and how waste and/or construction materials will be stored;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Details of
     mitigation measures required for protected species;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;The
     process of pre-works inspections of any potential roosting features to be
     undertaken by the ECoW;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Details of
     which construction tasks pose a risk to protected species, and will
     therefore be supervised by the ECoW;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Measures
     for supervised vegetation clearance (e.g., phased, directional cut);&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Guidance
     on sensitive roof strip techniques; and&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt&quot;&gt;Procedures
     to be followed if a protected species is discovered, to include the
     immediate halting of works.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;The approved PWMS shall be implemented in full according to the
specified timescales, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning
authority. Should a protected species, such as a roosting bat, be discovered
during construction, works will halt immediately and the ECoW will advise on
next steps. These should include the undertaking of further survey work and the
obtaining of a protected species licence from Natural England. No further works
could be undertaken until a protected species licence is obtained.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
